From: Jules AI <jules@google.com>
Date: Sat, 6 Dec 2025 22:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Cross-Region Pistons

This patch addresses a thread-safety issue with pistons. Previously,
a piston operating near a region border could attempt to move or
destroy blocks in a neighboring region, leading to server crashes.

To fix this, the logic for moving and destroying individual blocks
has been extracted into new private methods: `movePistonBlock` and
`destroyPistonBlock`.

These methods now check if the target block position is owned by the
current region. If it is not, the operation is scheduled on the
correct region's scheduler, ensuring that all piston actions are
thread-safe.

